From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:16:01 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 21/23] fix(mpeg): end a movie at its sequence end and publish
 it where games look

Two ways a movie never ended:

- The end was only taken from a disc stream EOF, which comes when the
  stream reaches its end LBN. Games stop reading once only a partial
  last sector is left (SLES-55605 treats <= 4 bytes as done), so it never
  came and sceMpegGetPicture waited for pictures forever. A movie now
  also ends once its sequence_end_code has been demuxed in this stream
  generation, every byte read has been demuxed and nothing is buffered.
- Games inline sceMpegIsEnd as a read of the first word of libmpeg's
  state behind sceMpeg+0x40, so the stub's own IsEnd is never called and
  nothing set that word. GetPicture now sets it once the movie is over,
  by the same rule the stub's IsEnd uses.

Also: uncapped [MPEG:status] and [CdSt:status] lines every 120 VSync
ticks, since the per-event traces stop after 32 lines and made a slow
movie look stalled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
